ics the administrators  were employed much like teachers and  doctors since they were employed through  the warehouse they also created a  canteen for their food supply to make  life easier for themselves this  warehouse administrator system worked  relatively well in the meantime the  village now a proper town was fully  covered with public utilities this was  facilitated by specialists having direct  and easy access to needed materials  through the warehouse instead of having  to get them individually from different  people from different parts of town this  gave people an idea since it worked so  well with utilities what if everything  was done through the warehouse on their  next meeting they agreed to trade for  computer equipment and hired an i.t  professional who created carlstot's very  own personalized demand and supply  network which sped up administration by  an order of magnitude the warehouse  canteen initially created to serve the  administrators became more and more  popular with the rest of the town  especially now that a cook was working  there full time with the canteen  services people could save a lot of time  since now they didn't have to bother  with cooking as much a food selection  system was integrated into the  personalized demand and supply network  so everyone could put together meals  most suitable for them depending on what  ingredients were available with time  people specialized more and more on  certain tasks these specialists created  workshop cooperatives where all members  were shareholders which allowed them to  share their knowledge and experience  freely since those can't be monopolized  either consequently the quality and  quantity of goods produced increased  significantly to help keep knowledge and  experience freely available to anyone in  the free market they even created a  public library and an open source  knowledge database where anyone could  upload what they wanted pending a public  review after months of struggle to  rebuild their lives the end caps of  colorstat succeeded in reaching what  they would call an ancap utopia or at  least the beginnings of it theirs was a  society free of coercion and oppression  without a government without a  monopolistic ruling class and without  traditional currency also known as  communism  but before any tankies would get too  excited no the soviet union wasn't  communist and it never even came close  to achieving communism it was a state  capitalist oligarchy run by dictators  but that will be the topic of another  video in the meantime thank you for  watching check out my patreon if you  want to support my channel and also  don't forget to like and subscribe and  i'll be seeing you next time

